    "text": {
     "en": "Rounding gives a close easy number. We round to the nearest ten, hundred or thousand.\nIf the ones digit is 5 or more, round the tens up. 348 is about 350 to the nearest ten.\nTo the nearest hundred, 348 is about 300 because 48 is less than 50.\nExpanded form shows value of each digit: 3,425 = 3000 + 400 + 20 + 5.\nRounding is useful when we only need an estimate."
    }
